 //! separate routes rather than content negotiation on `/zk/` and
 //! `/zk/result/:id`, so a machine consumer that forgets an `Accept` header can
 //! never be served a web page instead of the data it asked for.
+//!
+//! The blind-relay path (`crate::relay`) is wired the same way: its own
+//! request-creation endpoint, responses on the SAME `POST /response/:id`, and a
+//! pickup endpoint instead of a verification outcome, because the service holds
+//! no key that could open the response.
+//!
+//! - `POST /relay/request`         create a request encrypted to the CLIENT's key
+//! - `GET  /relay/status/:id`      pending | responded | picked_up
+//! - `GET  /relay/response/:id`    the stored JWE, once, to the pickup-token holder
 
